{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510695-wolves-in-sheep-s-clothing-potential","id":1510695,"title":"Wolves in sheep's clothing potential","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-04T05:41:23-07:00","id":1510695,"title":"Wolves in sheep's clothing potential","content":"I found quite interesting the concept of ghouls who steals and transplant vampiric parts using surgery and hedge magic, as presented in the third issue of the comic Winter's Teeth.<br /> Some questions arise:<br /> <br /> 1- would these ghouls require mortal blood, or more Vitae, to sustain those stolen parts?<br /> 2- would those parts be vulnerable to sunlight ( and more vulnerable than normal to fire ) ?<br /> 3- what could be the benefits of stealing body parts from a lower generation vampire?<br /> <br /> And finally, what would happen to a ghoul that manages to replace almost all his living body with vampiric parts?<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> Side question: mabye dhampir and revenant parts could be stolen too - expecially bone marrow for the quasi-vitae production?<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> Another side question: if a ghoul somehow manages to learn the basics of Vicissitude, could he shape and mold those stolen parts more harmoniously in his body so he doesn't look like Frankenstein?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 05-04-2023, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T16:55:47-07:00","id":1510735,"title":"","content":"Overall, I would say the Dhampir parts would be better for the surgical scenario since they are alive by default.<br /> <br /> The issue with vampire parts is that they are supposed to turn to ash/rot as soon as they are separated from the body, generally vampires regrow parts rather than reattaching them. Overcoming that aspect would take true magic or high-end Thaumaturgy. For context, it takes rank five Serpentis to allow a vampire heart to leave the body without harm to itself or the target. Hedge Magic overall is weaker than disciplines.<br /> <br /> As for what happens to the transplant recipient, assuming you can procure enough Dhampirs to farm organs, I would lean towards the notion that very bad things will happen to them. While Vitae can be used by anyone, actual organs are a different matter, tissue rejection becomes the main issue here. Yes you can hand wave the mundane forms of tissue rejection with hedge magic, but I am also considering the supernatural forms of tissue rejection. Dhampirs of different heritages can mean the magic fights with each other inside the body. <br /> <br /> The potential internal alchemical explosions produced by mixing cainite dhampir parts and Kuei-jin sired dhampir parts is the true crazy scenario, joss verses vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T06:09:17-07:00","id":1510876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The issue with vampire parts is that they are supposed to turn to ash/rot as soon as they are separated from the body, generally vampires regrow parts rather than reattaching them. Overcoming that aspect would take true magic or high-end Thaumaturgy. For context, it takes rank five Serpentis to allow a vampire heart to leave the body without harm to itself or the target. Hedge Magic overall is weaker than disciplines. </div> </div> </div>In the comic Winter's teeth , that is based on V5 rules, hedge wizard ghoul-surgeons manage to do that, in issue 3. There is even a section at the end of the issue which explains it from a rule viewpoint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://readcomiconline.li/Comic/Vampire-The-Masquerade-Winter-s-Teeth/Issue-3?id=181172\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://readcomiconline.li/Comic/Vampire-The-Masquerade-Winter-s-Teeth/Issue-3?id=181172\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://readcomiconline.li/Comic/Vampire-The-Masquerade-Winter-s-Teeth/Issue-3?id=181172\" target=\"_blank\"> https://readcomiconline.li/Comic/Vampire-The-Masquerade-Winter-s-Teeth/Issue-3?id=181172 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> There's a Vicissitude power ( Vicissitude 6 ) &quot;Graft Life to Life&quot; who allows to attach living parts to mortal, ghouls... or vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"http://maierstorm.org/Vampire/index.php/Vicissitude\" target=\"_blank\">Vicissitude</a> 6<br /> With normal Vicissitude, a Tzimisce may take the arm from one person and graft it to another, but the recipient is unable to control the arm and it soon begins to decay. With this power, the user may take body parts from living creatures and graft them on to others, living or undead, and allow for the recipient to use the new limb. Exceptionally monstrous and disturbing creatures can be created with this power or one may graft extra organs into others, allowing them to function longer while wounded.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> Removing a limb requires an Intelligence + Body Crafts roll (difficulty 6). Extracting an organ is an extended Intelligence + Body Crafts roll (difficulty 7), with 10 successes required and each roll representing an hour of work. The process of grafting must then begin within an hour. or the limb or organ dies. Attachment is an extended roll of Intelligence + Body Crafts (difficulty 7), requiring 10 successes and each roll representing half an hour's work. Attaching an appropriate limb, such as a human arm to a human, is difficulty 7. Attaching an inappropriate limb, such as horse legs to a human, is difficulty 8. Inserting organs is difficulty 9. Attaching limbs to a vampire is somewhat easier (difficulty 6). Theoretically, one could put organs inside a vampire, but this has no effect.<br /> <br /> The effect of attaching extra limbs is entirely up to the Storyteller. Extra arms might help in grappling and multiple attacks and extra legs might aid stability but the main effect is generally freakishness rather than effectiveness, since coordinating the extra limbs is very difficult. Extra organs grant the recipient an additional wounded health level per organ, though a maximum of two can be grafted.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div><br /> But what happens to a living part attached to a vampire's body? Does it require oxygen, nutrients ecc.? Is it vulnerable to sunlight? Is it kept in &quot;stasis&quot; by the power of Blood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 05-06-2023, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}